  <layout>One page of verse, one column, centred in the text block. Running head at top centre with the page number at top left. Show-through from the facing page in the right margin, not transcribed. Catchword "Hac" at the lower right, outside the text block.</layout>
  <page_number>66</page_number>
  <running_head>GVISIACA</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Hac</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Qui cuncta rubri fulminis ignibus</l>
    <l n="2">Terret caducis, quum ferit arduus</l>
    <l n="3">Titanas Ætneos, minasq;</l>
    <l n="4">Centimanas cohibet Gigantum:</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Te perduelli cum grege turpium</l>
    <l n="6">Perdet virorum, Barbare, Gallicæ</l>
    <l n="7">Fatale monstrum Gentis, atque</l>
    <l n="8">Innocuo rutilans cruore</l>
    <l n="9">Immanis, eheu! bellua, quæ bonos</l>
    <l n="10">Summi sequentes dogmata Numinis</l>
    <l n="11">Virgis cruentas, igne torres,</l>
    <l n="12">Et cruciibus lacerasq; ferro.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Verum reteEtis [?] Guisiadum dolis,</l>
    <l n="14">Quæ nunc Nauarrum Gallia principem</l>
    <l n="15">Virtute sublimi decorum</l>
    <l n="16">Marte ferox petit impotente,</l>
    <l n="17">Tandem secundo Numine sospitem,</l>
    <l n="18">Pacata, iustis reddet honoribus,</l>
    <l n="19">Et proximis regi benigna</l>
    <l n="20">Sedibus egregium reponet.</l>
    <l n="21" para="true">Quem nunc cruentis fraudibus explicat,</l>
    <l n="22">Et præp̄ [?] aratis mortibus eximit,</l>
    <l n="23">Cunctisq; seruatum periclis</l>
    <l n="24">Incolumem fouet aduocata</l>
    <l n="25">Christi potentis dextera vindicis.</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">Hæ sola vires subruit impias.</l>
    <l n="27">Hæc tela coniurata rumpit</l>
    <l n="28">Sacrilegæ potior caterua,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Show-through from the facing page on the right margin ignored. The word "reteEtis" is read as "retectis" with doubt; "cruciibus" and "præp̄" are uncertain readings; the line "Et præp̄ aratis" is partly abbreviated and may be illegible. The Æ in "Ætneos" and the q; abbreviations are kept as printed. The verse lines are joined within each stanza; the stanza breaks follow the indentation.</notes>
</page>
